- wiki_breadcrumbs = admin_knowledge_breadcrumbs(mode: :formatting_guide)

- content_for :admin_actions do
  = link_to 'All pages', admin_wiki_pages_path, class: 'btn btn-line-light btn-sm'

= render 'shared/admin_page', page_title: 'Knowledge formatting guide', current_page: 'Formatting guide', document_title: 'Knowledge formatting guide - Admin', breadcrumbs: wiki_breadcrumbs, page_subtitle: 'How to write pages, use the editor, and link between them.' do
  div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(260px,1fr) minmax(0,2fr);gap:22px;align-items:start"
    .admin-stack
      = render 'sidebar', current_page: nil
    .admin-stack
      .admin-panel
        h2 Editor (Trix)

        p
          | The content area is a rich text editor. Use the toolbar for
          strong  bold
          | ,
          em  italic
          | , headings, bullet and numbered lists, quotes, code, links, and file attachments (images and documents upload through the paperclip icon).

        p
          strong  External links:
          |  Use the link button and paste a full URL (
          code.admin-mono https://…
          | ). Those open like normal web links.

        h2 style="margin-top:40px" Internal wiki links

        p
          | To point readers at another knowledge page
          strong  without typing the site URL
          | , use double square brackets. The site turns these into links when someone
          strong  views
          |  the page (they stay as plain text while you edit).

        h3 style="margin-top:24px" Page paths

        p
          | Each page sits in the tree under an optional parent. Its wiki path is slugs joined with
          code.admin-mono /
          | , for example
          code.admin-mono boards/baldrick8
          |  for “Baldrick8” under “Boards”. Root pages are a single segment. When you view a page, copy the exact
          code.admin-mono
            | [[…]]
          |  line under the title.

        h3 style="margin-top:24px" Syntax

        .admin-table-wrap
          table.admin-table
            thead
              tr
                th Write
                th Meaning
            tbody
              tr
                td
                  code.admin-mono
                    | [[parent-slug/child-slug]]
                td
                  | Link to a nested page using each segment’s slug from the root down (same order as in the wiki link under that page’s title).
              tr
                td
                  code.admin-mono
                    | [[page-slug]]
                td
                  | Link using the page’s slug alone when that’s enough—usually the last segment of its wiki path (see the line under the title when you view that page). Slugs are unique among siblings; use a multi-segment path when the same slug exists under different parents.
              tr
                td
                  code.admin-mono
                    | [[Page title]]
                td
                  | Link by
                  strong title
                  | , case-insensitive. If two pages share the same title, the first match wins—prefer a slug in that case.
              tr
                td
                  code.admin-mono
                    | [[slug|Label shown]]
                td
                  | Same as a slug or title link, but the visible text is
                  strong Label shown
                  |  (MediaWiki-style:
                  code.admin-mono target|label
                  | ).

        h3 style="margin-top:24px" Where markers work

        ul style="padding-left:1.25rem;margin:0 0 1rem"
          li Normal paragraphs and most body text.
          li
            strong Not
            |  expanded inside preformatted or code blocks, inside existing hyperlinks, or in a few other special regions—so you can show literal
            code.admin-mono
              | [[brackets]]
            |  in examples if you put them in a preformatted block.

        h3 style="margin-top:24px" Broken links

        p
          | If nothing matches yet, the text appears as an
          strong amber, dotted underline
          |  link. Click it to open “New page” with title (and parent, when the link looks like a path) prefilled so you can add content and save.

        p
          | If you prefer not to create the page, adjust the bracket text in the editor instead.

        h2 style="margin-top:40px" Page tree

        ul style="padding-left:1.25rem;margin:0 0 1rem"
          li
            strong  Parent page
            |  — choose a parent to nest this page under the sidebar. Leave as “Top level” for a root page.
          li
            strong  Position
            |  — lower numbers sort earlier among siblings in the sidebar.

        p style="margin-top:24px"
          = link_to 'Back to knowledge home', admin_wiki_pages_path, class: 'lnk'
